    "explanationEn": "Jack should digitally sign the file and provide his public key to the other organization. This will allow them to validate his signature, as well as the integrity of the signed file.Chapter 1: Domain 1.0: General Security Concepts 227 Encrypting the file does not ensure its integrity but does protect its confidentiality. Sending a hash does not ensure that the email was not modified, and emailing file size and name does not ensure the file was not changed."
