    "answer": 3,
    "explanationFr": "Encryption is used to preserve confidentiality. Availability controls work to ensure that assets remain accessible and usable, and encryption can actually work against this in some circumstances, such as if a key is lost or the encrypted file becomes corrupted. Encryption is not used directly to preserve least privilege, nor does it preserve physical security.242 Appendix ■",
    "explanationEn": "Encryption is used to preserve confidentiality. Availability controls work to ensure that assets remain accessible and usable, and encryption can actually work against this in some circumstances, such as if a key is lost or the encrypted file becomes corrupted. Encryption is not used directly to preserve least privilege, nor does it preserve physical security.242 Appendix ■"
