    "explanationEn": "The most common motivation for hacktivists is to make a political statement. Reputational gains are often associated with unskilled attackers/script kiddies, whereas financial gain is most commonly a goal of organized crime or insider threats. Gathering high-value data is typical of both nation-state actors and organized crime."
