    "explanationEn": "Air gapping refers to the server not being on a network. This means literally that there is “air” between the server and the network. This prevents malware from infecting the backup server. A separate virtual local area network (VLAN) or physical network segment can256 Appendix ■ enhance security but is not as effective as air gapping. A honeynet is used to detect attacks against a network, but it doesn’t provide effective defense against malware in this scenario."
