    "explanationEn": "A microservice architecture builds applications as a set of loosely coupled services that provide specific functions using lightweight protocols. It doesn’t specifically define the size of the systems, but it is not a tightly coupled environment. Protocol choice is often open standards–based, but the emphasis is on lightweight protocols. There is not a requirement that services be in-house or third party exclusively."
