    "explanationEn": "The correct answer is to encrypt all the web traffic to this application using Transport Layer Security (TLS). This is one of the most fundamental security steps to take with any website. A web application firewall (WAF) is probably a good idea, but it is not the most important thing for Ryan to implement. While a network-based intrusion prevention system (NIPS) or network-based intrusion detection system (NIDS) may be a good idea, those should be considered after TLS is configured."
