    "explanationEn": "Data sovereignty means that governments have the ability to control data within their borders via law and regulations. Theresa’s organization will need to comply with the laws of each country they operate in. Obfuscation refers to making something difficult to understand or read. Legal holds are used to require preservation of data when legal action is occurring or pending. Geographic restriction is used to limit where data can be accessed from and is a technical control used by organizations as part of data security efforts."
