    "answer": 0,
    "explanationFr": "Caroline should select ISO 27002. ISO 27002 is an international standard for implementing and maintaining information security systems. ISO 27701 is an international standard security technique for privacy information management systems; NIST 800-12 is a general security standard and it is a US standard, not an international one; and NIST 800-53 is a collection of security and privacy controls for information systems and organizations.",
    "explanationEn": "Caroline should select ISO 27002. ISO 27002 is an international standard for implementing and maintaining information security systems. ISO 27701 is an international standard security technique for privacy information management systems; NIST 800-12 is a general security standard and it is a US standard, not an international one; and NIST 800-53 is a collection of security and privacy controls for information systems and organizations."
