    "explanationEn": "Organizations typically establish KPIs (key performance indicators), which may be described in MSAs (master service agreements), SLAs (service level agreements), or SOWs (statements of work). These help to measure and monitor the vendor’s performance. MOUs are used to document how organizations want to work together, not to establish performance measures. Compliance audits and regulatory requirements are only part of performance management."
